{
  "description": "A compatibility-preserving diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec. DiagnosisProbe(view, device) exposes run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions while inspecting the actual trained model through architecture-appropriate probes.",
  "motivation": "Support model diagnosis and iterative improvement under the shared RecHarness benchmark using only observed public data and a consistent validation objective.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain the DiagnosisProbe interface and SASRec compatibility methods: item_emb, log2feats, predict_score, user_train, meta_data, and review_data. Adapt probes when the architecture changes. Training batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L. Use only interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; mark unavailable review information and simulator traits as unobserved. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for 20 real training users, five per category. Rank trials by macro-average validation HR@10 across all four datasets. Preserve dataset routing, prescribed seeds, and the host evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    initialize(view, device):\n        store view and device\n        bind architecture-compatible probes to view.model\n\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set model to evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            inspect valid sequence positions in training batches\n            compute supported diagnostics from model outputs and observed data\n            generate unseen-item recommendations for five training users per category\n        restore model training state\n        return metrics, metric_definitions\n\nSelect trial using host-computed macro validation HR@10.",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Combines a stable diagnostic interface with explicit data-availability constraints and benchmark-aligned selection.",
    "negative": "Describes an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or diagnostic method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support comparable diagnosis across architecture changes and guide subsequent model improvements.",
    "negative": "Its value depends on defining informative probes and showing that diagnosis-guided changes improve validation performance."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces, batch structure, available data, and selection metric are clearly specified.",
    "negative": "Architecture adaptation, padding-aware diagnostics, and full-catalog recommendation generation require careful implementation."
  }
}
